===Etymology 3===
Shortened from {{m|en|sol}}, to make it an [[open syllable]] for uniformity with the rest of the scale, from Glover's [[solmization]], from {{inh|en|enm|sol||fifth degree or note of Guido of Arezzo's hexachordal scales}}, {{der|en|it|sol}} in the solmization of Guido of Arezzo, from the first syllable of {{der|en|la|solve|t=wash away}} in the lyrics of the scale-ascending hymn ''{{w|Ut queant laxis}}'' by Paulus Deacon.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|music}} A syllable used in [[solfège]] to represent the fifth note of a [[major scale]].
## {{lb|en|shapenote}} Sometimes syllable for both the second and the fifth.

